      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refshale%C3%B8en%2C_Copenhagen",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Burmeister & Wain shipyard operated there for over a century, employing 8,000 at its peak.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refshale%C3%B8en%2C_Copenhagen",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the shipyard closed in 1996, the abandoned buildings became a mix of creative studios, flea markets, and storage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refshale%C3%B8en%2C_Copenhagen",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Since 2018, the island hosts Reffen, Northern Europe's largest street‑food market with 40 restaurants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refshale%C3%B8en%2C_Copenhagen",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The volunteer spaceflight group Copenhagen Suborbitals now operates from the former shipyard.",
